  "definition": "Huntington's disease is an inherited, progressively worsening brain disorder that can begin at any age and causes movement and coordination problems, such as involuntary movements and trouble with walking, speaking, or swallowing. It also leads to declining mental abilities and can involve psychiatric difficulties.",
